    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>scala_function</b>: a Scala 3 "write a function (or class)" question type.</p>
<p>The student's answer contains top-level Scala 3 definitions (functions, classes, objects,
case classes, enums...). Each test's <em>test code</em> is a block of Scala statements that is
run inside a test <code>@main</code> method, typically printing a result, e.g.
<code>println(square(3))</code>, compared exactly with the expected output.</p>
<p>All tests are run in a single Jobe job (combinator template) to avoid repeated Scala
compilation; if that run fails (e.g. an exception) CodeRunner reruns the tests one at a time.
Tests that use standard input are always run one at a time.</p>
<p>Compiler warnings do not fail an answer. To make them fatal, set the sandbox parameters to
<code>{"compileargs": ["-Werror"]}</code>.</p>]]></text>
